{"id": "EUVD-2026-64379", "enisaUuid": "7e56eb88-78ac-3c83-92da-a13a8f514e73", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/smc: fix TOCTOU race between smc_listen_out() and listener close\n\nsmc_listen_out() reads lsmc->sk.sk_state without the listener lock,\nthen acquires lock_sock_nested() only after the check passes. This\nopens a window where smc_close_active() can transition the listener\nto SMC_CLOSED, call smc_close_cleanup_listen() to drain the accept\nqueue, and release the lock, all between the lockless read and the\ndelayed lock acquisition:\n\n  smc_listen_work (smc_hs_wq)          smc_close_active()\n  -------------------------------      -------------------------\n  release_sock(child)\n  if (sk_state == SMC_LISTEN) TRUE\n                                        lock_sock(listener)\n                                        sk_state = SMC_CLOSED\n                                        smc_close_cleanup_listen()\n                                        release_sock(listener)\n                                        flush_work(tcp_listen_work)\n  lock_sock_nested(listener)\n  smc_accept_enqueue(listener, child) /* child enqueued on dead listener */\n\nsmc_close_active() flushes only tcp_listen_work. Work items already\ndispatched onto smc_hs_wq for the CLC handshake continue running\nunguarded. smc_accept_enqueue() takes a sock_hold() on the child that\nis never released, so the child smc_sock, its clcsock, and the\nreference all leak. A remote peer that opens TCP connections while the\nserver calls close() can exhaust kernel memory.\n\nMove lock_sock_nested() to before the sk_state check so that the test\nand the enqueue are atomic under the listener lock.", "datePublished": "2026-08-22T15:32:55", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:16:09", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/53c7938d8bcfde3296ec1a347ba2a9393c1fdcfa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/feb71634bb1abab3e8fb5cde874b27001cc1282e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/01865e1ddb126b25ac9eba5cdd7ec49e11183a64", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/00f89433777236ced4771211047fb5d4cd581cea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/78e5ebcd1c10ed7c8bda0a99e0abd5b62da86d67", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ff5bcd804b5bc5c64736b7d318c20e12ea9506b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/185a4caeecabc150106deda1da170b09f2ad803f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74692", "GHSA-r9r5-95ff-67hq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.49, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11849525-44fa-3f0b-af1d-7f297d5f455b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fd57770dd198f5b2ddd5b9e6bf282cf98d63adb9 <00f89433777236ced4771211047fb5d4cd581cea"}, {"id": "1d4dcd86-caba-3b31-ba30-f30c73209b2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fd57770dd198f5b2ddd5b9e6bf282cf98d63adb9 <ff5bcd804b5bc5c64736b7d318c20e12ea9506b8"}, {"id": "1f495ad9-7f5d-332c-a028-1187f29c25f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.19.299 <4.20"}, {"id": "2419c082-1e31-30df-b899-64f075c74197", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.152"}, {"id": "726f61f5-5d7b-302a-8f3d-7a8a55520008", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.45"}, {"id": "75f66882-0830-32f2-88ff-dd65d65858e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.1"}, {"id": "7d1def3b-4b6b-3062-9703-db189ae582cb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.104"}, {"id": "7e961d75-1cef-303b-9d41-6d4050d4b7bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fd57770dd198f5b2ddd5b9e6bf282cf98d63adb9 <01865e1ddb126b25ac9eba5cdd7ec49e11183a64"}, {"id": "9c5de05b-4143-31ae-90e4-e2cc2def897d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fd57770dd198f5b2ddd5b9e6bf282cf98d63adb9 <78e5ebcd1c10ed7c8bda0a99e0abd5b62da86d67"}, {"id": "a0036830-53e4-3a69-9937-d8df7e7b065a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.216"}, {"id": "a97e41e4-e8c4-3dc0-9610-8bceac1cd24d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d1d004585b40c212b338fc8a40cbaaf230ea4703"}, {"id": "adda7fe2-f38a-3aa8-8a7c-112b5ee6c061", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fd57770dd198f5b2ddd5b9e6bf282cf98d63adb9 <185a4caeecabc150106deda1da170b09f2ad803f"}, {"id": "b8908d30-d879-30a8-9068-bfcbc011c92e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fd57770dd198f5b2ddd5b9e6bf282cf98d63adb9 <53c7938d8bcfde3296ec1a347ba2a9393c1fdcfa"}, {"id": "c24d74c1-1490-3863-b3aa-54034dc0785d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "cdbb2bb6-ce80-389c-9e31-6265b35ba33a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fd57770dd198f5b2ddd5b9e6bf282cf98d63adb9 <feb71634bb1abab3e8fb5cde874b27001cc1282e"}, {"id": "d4f7b89e-efda-3804-a1b9-fcb49433d7fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.9"}, {"id": "d8c1bef1-90e4-329f-97eb-d7e8465692c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e368009a-7d5e-3df8-83ca-add31e2092f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.183"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b892ba3f-c1ef-3bfe-b957-33085684bc86", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}